size-buffers: fluid model in 10 us steps. Illustrative, not a measurement.
stack             kernel
arrival           idle 0.000 Mpps, burst 4.000 Mpps for 1500 us from 500 us
stage 1           RX ring: 512 packets, drained at 1.500 Mpps
stage 2           socket buffer: 92 packets (212992 B at 2304 B each), read at 1.000 Mpps
reader pause      none

dropped, stage 1  3238 packets (rx_missed_errors)
dropped, stage 2  828 packets (UdpRcvbufErrors)
first drop        stage 2 at 680 us
peak fill         stage 1: 512 of 512, stage 2: 92 of 92

To lose nothing in this scenario:
ring              3750 packets, 7500 KiB per queue at 2048 B
socket buffer     2000 packets, 4608000 B, SO_RCVBUF request 2250 KiB
ring memory now   1024 KiB per queue, 1024 KiB for 1 queue(s)
